  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Coffee Farmer Livelihoods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Coffee Farmers
- Schools
- Smallholder farmers
- Coffee companies</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing child labour through seeds for education and improved income in Uganda</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than 1.8 million smallholder farmers in Uganda depend on coffee for their livelihoods. In fact, Uganda is the second largest coffee producer in Africa, and the eighth largest worldwide producing about 10 percent of the world&#x2019;s coffee supply. The increasing child labour on Uganda coffee farms threatens to taint Uganda&#x2019;s key export commodity, upon which the country relies for around a quarter of its foreign revenue earnings.</narrative>
  </description>
